From 7a0dcd5fde2e90f1bc9f7650c964d6e791be2e11 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arena Agent <agent@arena.ai>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 16:23:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 24/29] The importer can hold a driver's own dependencies, and
 knows what a driver drives

Two gaps, found by reading the code instead of the description of it. The task said
LinuxVulkanDriverManager "only recognises libvulkan_freedreno*/libvulkan_panfrost*" - it does not:
isMainLibrary accepts any libvulkan_*.so, so a Mesa lavapipe zip imports and works today. What it
cannot do is carry a second file, and lavapipe needs one: Mesa links against libLLVM.so.19.1, and
once the importer renames the driver to its own LIB_NAME and drops everything else from the archive,
the driver dlopens into "libLLVM.so.19.1 not found" thirty seconds into a session, inside the guest,
with nothing in the log to say why.

  - isCompanionLibrary: a versioned soname, nothing else (rejects .so.txt and friends), and never the
    main library or the PanVK backend - those keep their own rules.
  - the archive loop copies companions beside the driver, same per-library cap, duplicates refused.
  - adopt() checks each one with the two rules already used for the driver (AArch64, glibc) and then
    reconciles the set against meta.json's "companions" list in both directions: companions present
    but undeclared is a refusal, a declared one missing is a refusal. Files next to a library the
    Vulkan loader will dlopen are not taken on trust from a zip someone found.
  - gpuVendor(sourceLibraryName): "software" / "mali" / "adreno". It has to be read from the name in
    the zip because the name on disk is the same for every driver, which is also why a software
    driver is otherwise indistinguishable from Turnip after import. Recorded in meta.json and exposed
    as getGpuVendor / isSoftwareDriver / softwareDriverIds for the Auto logic in the next commit.

No DT_RUNPATH parsing in the app: whether the driver actually looks beside itself is decided by
patchelf in the packaging step, which is where it can be verified once with readelf instead of
guessed at here with a hand-written ELF reader.

DriverArchivePolicyTest covers the vendor table and the companion shape, including the two names that
must not be accepted as companions. Note for whoever runs this: CI does not execute unit tests -
tools/build_local.sh only assembles - so a test task is being added in the packaging commit or these
assertions are decoration.

Co-authored-by: arena-agent <297053741+arena-agent@users.noreply.github.com>
